1
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,000
 Ryotsu! I'm back in training!

2
00:01:34,416 --> 00:01:36,692
 Good morning!

3
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,484
 There's nothing to be afraid of, right?

4
00:01:41,536 --> 00:01:44,000
 I'm not surprised all of a sudden.

5
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:46,458
 What's wrong, Ryo-chan? That head...

6
00:01:48,496 --> 00:01:50,000
 That's the truth.

7
00:01:52,786 --> 00:01:55,000
 Ryotsu borrowed money from the director!

8
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
He asked me with a serious
face, so I let him borrowed it.

9
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,460
I'm sure there will be a reward
next week, but Ryotsu didn't need it.

10
00:02:02,485 --> 00:02:04,283
 So how much did he borrow?

11
00:02:04,308 --> 00:02:06,443
 That's 70,000 yen.

12
00:02:06,495 --> 00:02:08,000
 70,000 yen!

13
00:02:09,973 --> 00:02:13,205
 Ouch! What are you doing all of a sudden?

14
00:02:13,537 --> 00:02:14,807
 Chief!

15
00:02:14,905 --> 00:02:17,000
 You bastard!

16
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,000
 It's terrible!

17
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:22,000
No matter how many directors there
are, I've never pulled it from behind!

18
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:24,000
 When did you call for a reward?

19
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,000
That's wrong. Maybe
it's my misunderstanding.

20
00:02:28,132 --> 00:02:30,339
 I'll call you even if you die!

21
00:02:32,332 --> 00:02:36,000
 Chief, today is more difficult than usual.

22
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:37,000
 Of course!

23
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:40,000
What's the point of lying to the
director and borrowing money?

24
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,785
 Lying to the director?

25
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,958
That's why you bought this
70,000 yen plastic model, right?

26
00:02:44,983 --> 00:02:47,975
- What?
- No, chief, don't misunderstand.

27
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:53,220
 I bought this with the money I saved.

28
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:55,000
 Sorry.

29
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:57,000
 Terai, hold your feet.

30
00:02:57,000 --> 00:02:58,306
 Nakagawa, arm.

31
00:02:58,331 --> 00:02:59,331
 Yes!

32
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,000
 What are you doing?

33
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,000
 Ouch!

34
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:10,000
You're going to be taken
to the temple from tomorrow.

35
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,886
Train at the temple for 10 days
and get rid of your greed for money.

36
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,308
 That's it.

37
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,925
 You're still the same, Ryo-chan.

38
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:36,000
 Thank you for your help.

39
00:03:36,308 --> 00:03:39,276
 Ryo-chan, why don't you ask for a favor?

40
00:03:39,328 --> 00:03:42,453
 I don't like training.

41
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:44,000
 Don't say that!

42
00:03:44,693 --> 00:03:46,413
 And what is this luggage?

43
00:03:46,438 --> 00:03:49,121
 This is for 10 days.

44
00:03:49,247 --> 00:03:52,375
 I can't sleep when I change my pillow.

45
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:55,000
 You're not going to the Amazon.

46
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,000
 Show me!

47
00:04:00,214 --> 00:04:05,558
Do you think you can
train with this luggage?

48
00:04:05,865 --> 00:04:12,037
That's why I want you to
be careful not to play with it.

49
00:04:12,062 --> 00:04:13,583
 Shut up!

50
00:04:13,796 --> 00:04:15,840
 I'll take it all to the temple.

51
00:04:15,865 --> 00:04:17,246
 I understand.

52
00:04:19,128 --> 00:04:21,975
I'm a man of my word. You
can take it back anytime.

53
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,000
 I can take it back anytime.

54
00:04:25,130 --> 00:04:26,281
 Ryo-chan.

55
00:04:26,364 --> 00:04:27,364
 Yes.

56
00:04:27,479 --> 00:04:31,725
I'll give you the name
Chin-Nen instead of Zoku-myo.

57
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:33,000
 Chin-Nen?

58
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
 Then I'll name you Sennen and Mannen..

59
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,000
 Yes.

60
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
 These two are the teachers of Chin-Nen.

61
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
 Let's start training.

62
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
 Thank you.

63
00:04:43,025 --> 00:04:44,025
 Ryo-chan.

64
00:04:44,429 --> 00:04:45,935
 Please.

65
00:04:55,078 --> 00:04:58,135
 We've been training for a week.

66
00:04:58,408 --> 00:04:59,726
 I'm sorry.

67
00:04:59,766 --> 00:05:00,810
 I'm Muenen.

68
00:05:00,835 --> 00:05:02,000
 Nice to meet you.

69
00:05:02,255 --> 00:05:04,784
 We're from the same family.

70
00:05:04,932 --> 00:05:06,250
 Let's get along.

71
00:05:06,275 --> 00:05:08,683
 Leave it to me.

72
00:05:08,708 --> 00:05:09,708
 Yes.

73
00:05:10,166 --> 00:05:13,855
Throw away your evil
thoughts and sit down.

74
00:05:13,911 --> 00:05:14,919
 Start!

75
00:05:32,447 --> 00:05:35,000
 You've been trapped.

76
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
 How do you know?

77
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:42,000
If you train like me, you'll
know what you're thinking.

78
00:05:43,384 --> 00:05:46,656
 You think I am lying, don't you?

79
00:05:46,832 --> 00:05:50,000
I don't think so.
Don't make it up.

80
00:05:50,426 --> 00:05:53,189
 How dare you talk back to me?

81
00:05:55,816 --> 00:05:57,000
 Good for you.

82
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
 Don't underestimate me.

83
00:06:03,983 --> 00:06:05,000
 Damn it.

84
00:06:07,769 --> 00:06:08,769
 Good for you.

85
00:06:09,136 --> 00:06:10,136
 Run away.

86
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,000
 You bastard.

87
00:06:20,000 --> 00:06:23,000
 I'll use the sword to defeat you.

88
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,000
 Don't go against me.

89
00:06:40,828 --> 00:06:42,357
 Damn it.

90
00:06:43,470 --> 00:06:45,000
 What are you doing?

91
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
 I thought my heart would stop.

92
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:49,000
Just get changed and let's go.

93
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:53,069
Unfortunately, I'm the manager,
so please take care of the corridor.

94
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
 Damn it.

95
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
 I thought I was in the wrong place.

96
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,000
 I'm in trouble.

97
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
 It's been a long time.

98
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:11,000
 The hall is in a big mess.

99
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:14,000
 The wall is more foggy.

100
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,500
 Wait, wait!

101
00:07:16,500 --> 00:07:19,757
If you keep doing that,
it'll take a lot of effort.

102
00:07:19,782 --> 00:07:20,782
 But...

103
00:07:28,010 --> 00:07:32,572
If you keep doing this,
you'll be finished in one try.

104
00:07:32,699 --> 00:07:36,007
You start from there,
and I'll start from here.

105
00:07:36,032 --> 00:07:37,039
 B-But...

106
00:07:37,064 --> 00:07:39,000
 If you do this, the tattari will...

107
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,447
 The tattari is scary, so you can't hit it.

108
00:07:41,472 --> 00:07:44,000
If you do it with full speed,
you can finish in 5 minutes.

109
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:45,500
 Go for it!

110
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:02,000
 What? You're done already?

111
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
 Yes, completely.

112
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
 Don't be stupid.

113
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,500
 You still have 5 minutes to go.

114
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:09,818
 So that's the end of it, nya.

115
00:08:09,847 --> 00:08:13,500
Alright, if you're going to
say that, I'll make sure of it.

116
00:08:13,500 --> 00:08:17,500
But if you're going to lie,
you'd better be prepared.

117
00:08:17,500 --> 00:08:18,500
 Yes, nya.

118
00:08:28,500 --> 00:08:30,228
 Here, eat, eat.

119
00:08:30,707 --> 00:08:32,000
 What is this?

120
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,500
 Is this all you have?

121
00:08:33,500 --> 00:08:35,500
 You only have rice wine and shinko.

122
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:37,500
 The temple is a sacred food,

123
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:39,500
 so we don't use meat or fish.

124
00:08:39,500 --> 00:08:42,500
With all the vegetables,
it's the same as kirigiri.

125
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:44,776
 How can you be so patient?

126
00:08:44,893 --> 00:08:46,500
 It can't be helped.

127
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,632
 This is training too.

128
00:08:47,657 --> 00:08:49,500
 Now, let's eat.

129
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:57,500
 I hid it in my pants and brought it in.

130
00:08:57,500 --> 00:08:59,500
 You guys can eat it too.

131
00:08:59,500 --> 00:09:00,500
 We can't.

132
00:09:00,525 --> 00:09:02,794
 Eating meat is forbidden.

133
00:09:02,897 --> 00:09:04,923
 We'll get punished.

134
00:09:05,500 --> 00:09:06,719
 Oh, right.

135
00:09:06,744 --> 00:09:09,268
 There's still a lot left.

136
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:17,500
If you guys don't eat
it, I'll eat it all by myself.

137
00:09:17,500 --> 00:09:19,500
 Let's eat.

138
00:09:23,480 --> 00:09:24,480
 It's delicious.

139
00:09:24,793 --> 00:09:27,315
 You guys really don't have to eat it.

140
00:09:28,773 --> 00:09:30,460
 Let's eat.

141
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:33,500
 Alright.

142
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:35,729
Humans have to be
honest with their desires.

143
00:09:35,754 --> 00:09:38,448
 You guys have a good eye.

144
00:09:42,763 --> 00:09:45,763
 What are you guys doing?

145
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:53,132
 I'm sorry, Senren.

146
00:09:53,157 --> 00:09:56,136
It's a pity that the guy
has a terrible feeling.

147
00:09:56,302 --> 00:10:00,554
I tried to stop them, but
they didn't listen to me.

148
00:10:00,579 --> 00:10:01,500
 No, this is...

149
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:02,956
 This is...

150
00:10:03,010 --> 00:10:03,821
 Shut up!

151
00:10:03,909 --> 00:10:06,042
 This is a crime against humans.

152
00:10:07,073 --> 00:10:08,669
 I'll take responsibility.

153
00:10:08,694 --> 00:10:11,126
You'll sit in the hallway until night.
Understood?

154
00:10:11,535 --> 00:10:12,512
 No way.

155
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:30,061
 Damn it.

156
00:10:30,086 --> 00:10:32,005
 My legs are stiff.

157
00:10:32,030 --> 00:10:34,866
I have nothing to do
but sit in the hallway.

158
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:38,500
 No radio, no TV.

159
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:39,500
 No manga.

160
00:10:39,500 --> 00:10:40,500
 Nothing.

161
00:10:40,500 --> 00:10:41,500
 I'm bored.

162
00:10:41,500 --> 00:10:42,500
 I'll just sleep.

163
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:43,500
 Is that it?

164
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:44,778
 I'm not kidding.

165
00:10:44,837 --> 00:10:47,298
If you don't sleep early, you'll
have a hard time tomorrow.

166
00:10:48,802 --> 00:10:50,500
I'm hungry.
I can't sleep.

167
00:10:50,745 --> 00:10:52,500
 Let's order sushi.

168
00:10:52,639 --> 00:10:54,500
 That's impossible.

169
00:10:54,500 --> 00:10:58,500
Even if we can order, we
can't deliver it to this temple.

170
00:10:58,500 --> 00:11:00,022
 The security is very tight.

171
00:11:00,047 --> 00:11:02,747
 Then let's go eat from here.

172
00:11:05,069 --> 00:11:06,069
 We can't go.

173
00:11:06,094 --> 00:11:07,094
 It's okay.

174
00:11:07,246 --> 00:11:08,246
 It's night.

175
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:17,500
 If we get through here, we'll be...

176
00:11:23,500 --> 00:11:24,500
 What's that?

177
00:11:24,500 --> 00:11:25,500
 A cat?

178
00:11:25,500 --> 00:11:27,500
 It's a big cat.

179
00:11:28,500 --> 00:11:30,500
 No way.

180
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:46,500
 We can't go this far.

181
00:12:04,500 --> 00:12:05,500
 Jin!

182
00:12:08,614 --> 00:12:10,049
 I won't forgive you for escaping.

183
00:12:10,137 --> 00:12:11,797
 Don't say that.

184
00:12:12,539 --> 00:12:14,961
 Do something about them.

185
00:12:26,500 --> 00:12:28,500
 Is Ryo-san not here?

186
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:31,792
I came here to listen to
the strategy of this game.

187
00:12:32,185 --> 00:12:33,213
 I'm sorry.

188
00:12:33,456 --> 00:12:35,694
 Ryo-chan is in training now.

189
00:12:37,285 --> 00:12:39,883
 Ryo-chan, you're popular.

190
00:12:39,961 --> 00:12:44,500
You've been teaching me how to repair
toys and how to play games since yesterday.

191
00:12:44,500 --> 00:12:46,500
 Kids often come to you.

192
00:12:46,850 --> 00:12:49,272
 Senpai, that's not good.

193
00:12:49,411 --> 00:12:50,411
 That's right.

194
00:12:52,037 --> 00:12:55,037
 What are you doing now, Ryo-chan?

195
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:02,827
 I'll leave the rest to you.

196
00:13:03,129 --> 00:13:04,500
 See you later.

197
00:13:05,141 --> 00:13:06,500
 See you later.

198
00:13:07,172 --> 00:13:08,500
 What happened?

199
00:13:08,675 --> 00:13:11,644
It seems that a great
monk has disappeared.

200
00:13:12,016 --> 00:13:14,500
He says that there are
many monks in Tokyo.

201
00:13:14,867 --> 00:13:15,867
 I did it!

202
00:13:15,942 --> 00:13:17,500
 I'm the only one today.

203
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:20,500
 Twist, twist.

204
00:13:20,500 --> 00:13:21,860
 Twist without bending.

205
00:13:21,885 --> 00:13:24,399
 But you have to do the training properly.

206
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:28,500
 Now, now.

207
00:13:28,500 --> 00:13:29,500
 This, this.

208
00:13:35,500 --> 00:13:37,500
 The radio was useful.

209
00:13:37,500 --> 00:13:40,500
 I was able to play with the money.

210
00:13:40,500 --> 00:13:42,500
I should have done
this from the beginning.

211
00:13:42,500 --> 00:13:44,500
 This is bad, this is bad.

212
00:13:46,500 --> 00:13:48,500
 What's wrong?

213
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:50,915
 There was an event at 10 o'clock today.

214
00:13:51,111 --> 00:13:53,117
 I thought it was tomorrow.

215
00:13:53,142 --> 00:13:54,500
 What did you say?

216
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:58,103
Why didn't you tell me
such an important thing?

217
00:13:58,767 --> 00:14:00,851
What should I do?
It's my responsibility.

218
00:14:00,924 --> 00:14:02,185
 Tell the lady.

219
00:14:02,487 --> 00:14:03,431
 Wait, wait.

220
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:08,500
I don't want to be punished
for being responsible.

221
00:14:08,500 --> 00:14:10,500
I'll tell her that I'm the
representative of the monk.

222
00:14:10,525 --> 00:14:11,843
 Jingen?

223
00:14:12,029 --> 00:14:13,500
 Are you okay?

224
00:14:14,226 --> 00:14:16,865
 I'm good at deceiving.

225
00:14:16,890 --> 00:14:17,890
 Leave it to me.

226
00:14:23,072 --> 00:14:25,500
How is it?
It's a monk, isn't it?

227
00:14:25,525 --> 00:14:26,983
 If you say so.

228
00:14:27,270 --> 00:14:28,490
 Then I'll go.

229
00:14:28,938 --> 00:14:30,405
 See you later.

230
00:14:47,878 --> 00:14:50,313
This is bad. If they
find out, I'll be dead.

231
00:14:50,337 --> 00:14:51,677
 Are you the monk ?

232
00:14:57,038 --> 00:14:59,050
 Please come here.

233
00:14:59,075 --> 00:15:00,075
 Yes, sir.

234
00:15:14,500 --> 00:15:15,500
 Damn it.

235
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:16,500
 This is bad.

236
00:15:35,359 --> 00:15:36,359
 That's all.

237
00:15:38,425 --> 00:15:39,240
 Sir.

238
00:15:39,265 --> 00:15:39,904
 Damn it.

239
00:15:39,929 --> 00:15:40,925
 Did they find out?

240
00:15:42,117 --> 00:15:43,275
 I'm impressed.

241
00:15:43,300 --> 00:15:45,798
 We don't know your religion.

242
00:15:48,464 --> 00:15:50,464
 Thank you.

243
00:15:50,489 --> 00:15:51,489
 You're welcome.

244
00:15:51,514 --> 00:15:52,514
 Well, then.

245
00:15:52,539 --> 00:15:53,539
 Amen.

246
00:15:53,564 --> 00:15:55,564
 I'll leave this to you.

247
00:16:07,224 --> 00:16:08,542
 I did it.

248
00:16:08,699 --> 00:16:10,500
 Monks' books are full of kanji.

249
00:16:10,500 --> 00:16:13,500
 They're useless for amateurs.

250
00:16:13,500 --> 00:16:14,500
 By the way,

251
00:16:14,500 --> 00:16:15,779
 How much did you pay me?

252
00:16:17,302 --> 00:16:18,738
 Wow.

253
00:16:19,173 --> 00:16:22,839
I didn't know I'd get
this much in one day.

254
00:16:25,109 --> 00:16:26,109
 Welcome back.

255
00:16:26,177 --> 00:16:27,177
 How was it?

256
00:16:27,324 --> 00:16:28,475
 It's perfect.

257
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:30,793
 I gave you a nice monk.

258
00:16:30,818 --> 00:16:32,165
 That's good.

259
00:16:32,190 --> 00:16:34,650
 Let's have a party.

260
00:16:34,675 --> 00:16:36,775
 Let's have sashimi for 10 people.

261
00:16:36,931 --> 00:16:39,685
 Let's have shikigaki for 10 people.

262
00:16:39,890 --> 00:16:42,331
Let's have a party before
the monks go home.

263
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:44,500
 But the money is...

264
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:45,500
 Idiot.

265
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:49,500
You can't think of being a monk
just because you want to be a monk.

266
00:16:49,714 --> 00:16:50,714
 Yes.

267
00:16:51,032 --> 00:16:52,976
 Monks can't be monks.

268
00:16:53,812 --> 00:16:57,458
 You can order as much beer as you want.

269
00:17:03,753 --> 00:17:05,466
 Cheers.

270
00:17:10,154 --> 00:17:12,500
 I'm drinking more than usual.

271
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:13,500
 That's good.

272
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:15,500
 You're wonderful.

273
00:17:16,999 --> 00:17:18,500
 A phone call.

274
00:17:18,500 --> 00:17:20,500
 Red Snake, come on.

275
00:17:20,500 --> 00:17:22,892
 Here, kiss of fire.

276
00:17:22,917 --> 00:17:26,023
 Yellow, why aren't you coming out?

277
00:17:26,062 --> 00:17:28,475
 There's no way I can do it.

278
00:17:28,982 --> 00:17:30,500
 You're the best.

279
00:17:31,160 --> 00:17:32,500
 Next time, you can't do anything.

280
00:17:32,500 --> 00:17:33,500
 What about me?

281
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:34,500
 That's right.

282
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:38,500
You can't be a monk if you
can't even do one of the shikigaki.

283
00:17:38,972 --> 00:17:40,759
 I'm in trouble.

284
00:17:40,915 --> 00:17:42,500
 What? Are you in trouble again?

285
00:17:42,500 --> 00:17:44,924
 Mr. Red Snake, Mr. Osho is...

286
00:17:44,949 --> 00:17:46,794
 Call me Osho.

287
00:17:47,585 --> 00:17:49,070
 Oh, Mr. Red Snake.

288
00:17:49,372 --> 00:17:51,500
 Mr. Osho's younger brother called me.

289
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:54,500
He said he couldn't go to the
shrine because he had a cold.

290
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:56,926
 He asked me to go instead.

291
00:17:56,951 --> 00:17:57,820
 All right.

292
00:17:57,917 --> 00:18:00,500
 If I go, answer me.

293
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:01,500
 Yes.

294
00:18:01,500 --> 00:18:04,158
 Mr. Osho, can I really go?

295
00:18:04,183 --> 00:18:05,281
 Leave it to me.

296
00:18:05,329 --> 00:18:07,500
 If you refuse to go, you'll be punished.

297
00:18:07,500 --> 00:18:10,890
You can't go against
the path of the Buddha.

298
00:18:10,915 --> 00:18:11,872
 That's right.

299
00:18:11,941 --> 00:18:14,500
 Everything is part of the training.

300
00:18:14,500 --> 00:18:16,500
 You guys follow me.

301
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:19,500
 How much will I get next time?

302
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:20,935
 Please wait.

303
00:18:33,874 --> 00:18:35,310
 I found it.

304
00:18:35,456 --> 00:18:37,078
 It's here, Mr. Red Snake.

305
00:18:47,478 --> 00:18:49,685
 Why is the chief here?

306
00:18:49,802 --> 00:18:52,292
 Mr. Osho, I've been waiting for you.

307
00:18:53,181 --> 00:18:54,006
 Oh, no.

308
00:18:54,031 --> 00:18:56,500
 It's the chief's older brother's house.

309
00:18:56,525 --> 00:18:58,611
 I'm sorry for being so busy.

310
00:18:58,884 --> 00:19:00,617
 Actually, I have something to do.

311
00:19:00,642 --> 00:19:01,500
 Hey.

312
00:19:01,500 --> 00:19:02,786
 Listen to me.

313
00:19:02,991 --> 00:19:04,261
 This is my younger brother.

314
00:19:04,500 --> 00:19:05,500
 Hello.

315
00:19:05,500 --> 00:19:08,684
This is Mr. Osho who came
as a substitute this time.

316
00:19:08,958 --> 00:19:10,500
 Thank you.

317
00:19:10,675 --> 00:19:12,268
 Thank you, too.

318
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:16,500
 See you later.

319
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:31,958
 I don't think I can get away with this.

320
00:19:32,593 --> 00:19:33,818
 What's wrong?

321
00:19:33,843 --> 00:19:35,078
 I was in a hurry.

322
00:19:35,103 --> 00:19:38,868
The bag with the money and
the bag with the party goods.

323
00:19:38,893 --> 00:19:39,893
 What?

324
00:19:40,083 --> 00:19:41,597
 Did you make a mistake?

325
00:19:41,622 --> 00:19:43,345
 But I can't go back.

326
00:19:43,538 --> 00:19:45,538
 I have to do something.

327
00:19:45,672 --> 00:19:46,519
 Yes.

328
00:20:08,500 --> 00:20:10,317
 They look alike.

329
00:20:10,342 --> 00:20:11,059
 What?

330
00:20:11,200 --> 00:20:12,710
 Please be quiet.

331
00:20:15,500 --> 00:20:18,237
 Even though we are from the same group,

332
00:20:18,262 --> 00:20:21,044
 we are a little different.

333
00:20:21,069 --> 00:20:22,069
 Please understand.

334
00:20:22,094 --> 00:20:25,259
You may feel that we are
a little faster than usual,

335
00:20:25,284 --> 00:20:28,081
but the content of our
conversation is getting deeper.

336
00:20:35,151 --> 00:20:36,665
 That's all.

337
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:41,500
They look alike.

338
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:42,500
Yes.

339
00:20:42,500 --> 00:20:46,500
He's a fool who can't do
anything because he's a ryozu.

340
00:20:48,138 --> 00:20:51,313
 That's why today is the blood donation service.

341
00:20:51,391 --> 00:20:53,500
 And today will continue.

342
00:20:53,500 --> 00:20:54,500
 Excuse me.

343
00:20:54,500 --> 00:20:56,500
 I need your help.

344
00:20:56,500 --> 00:20:57,500
 What?

345
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:59,500
 When you go up to the top of the hill,

346
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:02,500
 turn around three times and cry out.

347
00:21:02,500 --> 00:21:03,728
 What for?

348
00:21:03,855 --> 00:21:05,972
 I told you that we are different.

349
00:21:06,007 --> 00:21:06,982
 Do it.

350
00:21:07,010 --> 00:21:08,869
 You'll make a mistake.

351
00:21:08,894 --> 00:21:10,594
 I won't do as you say.

352
00:21:10,728 --> 00:21:12,078
 But, brother.

353
00:21:12,211 --> 00:21:13,504
 Just go.

354
00:21:17,056 --> 00:21:18,182
 Then I'll go.

355
00:21:24,500 --> 00:21:26,500
 Open your mouth wider.

356
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:28,500
 Open your mouth wider.

357
00:21:28,500 --> 00:21:30,500
 Do you understand?

358
00:21:30,500 --> 00:21:31,500
 No.

359
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:34,392
 You can't go back.

360
00:21:34,685 --> 00:21:36,500
 It hurts.

361
00:21:36,500 --> 00:21:38,500
 It doesn't hurt if you destroy the temple.

362
00:21:38,748 --> 00:21:41,424
Compared to being hit in the city,
it's not painful at all.

363
00:21:42,830 --> 00:21:45,789
 I remember something.

364
00:21:45,984 --> 00:21:48,500
 I hit a cute subordinate in the city.

365
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:52,791
If you don't confess,
you'll be punished.

366
00:21:55,500 --> 00:21:56,500
 That's right.

367
00:21:56,500 --> 00:21:58,182
 I remember it.

368
00:22:00,043 --> 00:22:01,639
 What's wrong, Daijiro?

369
00:22:01,678 --> 00:22:02,678
 Yes.

370
00:22:02,703 --> 00:22:04,500
 How terrible.

371
00:22:04,500 --> 00:22:08,230
Because of this person,
everyone may be punished.

372
00:22:10,232 --> 00:22:12,039
 Daijiro, I'm sorry.

373
00:22:12,064 --> 00:22:15,086
If you apologize in front of the
great monk who came from Shotenji,

374
00:22:15,111 --> 00:22:16,531
 you will be forgiven.

375
00:22:16,926 --> 00:22:18,590
Shotenji?

376
00:22:20,721 --> 00:22:22,385
 Excuse me.

377
00:22:22,410 --> 00:22:24,500
 Can you take off your glasses?

378
00:22:24,695 --> 00:22:26,500
 What are you talking about?

379
00:22:26,500 --> 00:22:29,065
 This is the characteristic of our sect.

380
00:22:29,090 --> 00:22:30,500
 It's absolutely useless.

381
00:22:31,990 --> 00:22:34,973
You.
Can't you listen to me?

382
00:22:34,998 --> 00:22:36,998
 I'll hit you seven times.

383
00:22:38,367 --> 00:22:40,174
 Hey, Daijiro.

384
00:22:40,262 --> 00:22:42,703
 Ryotsu, there's 10,000 yen down there.

385
00:22:42,761 --> 00:22:43,601
 Where?

386
00:22:43,689 --> 00:22:45,271
 Where is it?

387
00:22:50,398 --> 00:22:51,858
 Shotaimidari.

388
00:22:51,883 --> 00:22:54,139
 This is Ryotsu.

389
00:22:54,164 --> 00:22:56,199
 That's a big mistake.

390
00:22:56,238 --> 00:22:57,527
 Ryotsu.

391
00:22:58,045 --> 00:22:59,500
 Wait.

392
00:22:59,500 --> 00:23:01,500
 Stop it.

393
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:03,500
 What are you doing?

394
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:05,500
 What are you doing?

395
00:23:11,961 --> 00:23:14,094
 This is useless.

396
00:23:14,119 --> 00:23:15,500
 Shut up.

397
00:23:15,500 --> 00:23:17,195
 It's useless.

398
00:23:17,220 --> 00:23:18,933
 Stop it.

399
00:23:18,958 --> 00:23:21,414
 It's useless.

400
00:23:23,682 --> 00:23:27,432
In the temple,
there was a party

401
00:23:27,500 --> 00:23:29,570
 with sashimi and sukiyaki.

402
00:23:29,766 --> 00:23:31,650
 That's Ryotsu.

403
00:23:31,895 --> 00:23:33,598
 What about his training?

404
00:23:33,672 --> 00:23:35,928
I decided to stay in the
temple for the rest of my life.

405
00:23:37,418 --> 00:23:39,682
 Don't run away.

406
00:23:39,707 --> 00:23:41,836
 Go away.

407
00:23:42,002 --> 00:23:43,824
 Go away.

408
00:23:45,123 --> 00:23:47,868
If you want to eat,
you have to wait for the sun to set,

409
00:23:47,893 --> 00:23:49,893
 and the lion will become a cat again.

410
00:23:49,918 --> 00:23:51,763
 You don't have enough training.

411
00:23:51,788 --> 00:23:53,788
 Mr. Chinnen.

412
00:23:56,992 --> 00:23:59,560
 Help me.

413
00:24:05,500 --> 00:24:07,889
It's useless to stay in the
temple for seven hours.

414
00:24:07,914 --> 00:24:09,500
 I'm going to die.

415
00:24:09,549 --> 00:24:12,211
 I'll take care of it.

416
00:24:12,241 --> 00:24:14,116
 It's cheaper than the chief.

417
00:24:14,141 --> 00:24:15,785
 I'll find you a good house.

418
00:24:15,810 --> 00:24:18,481
 I'm a shopping professional.

419
00:24:18,510 --> 00:24:20,510
 Next time on My Home.

420
00:24:20,535 --> 00:24:21,918
 Thank you.

